// ---------------- Stories, part eight: the 88-rated tier ----------------
// Same shape as before: ST(id, logline, tagline, 'setting/tod/who/caption|...', 'trailer line|...'). Cast letters only
// where the catalogue has that actor in that slot.
ST('faust', "The devil wagers an archangel that he can corrupt a good man, sends a plague to a German town, and buys an old scholar's soul with the gift of youth.", "Heaven and hell bet on one man.", "village/n/A/a winged demon spreads his cloak over a whole town|village/n//the plague takes the town house by house|lab/n//an old scholar burns his books and calls on the dark|ballroom/d//a young man again, carried off on a flying cloak to a wedding feast|village/n//a girl in the snow holds her dead baby", "Mephisto made a wager.|One day of youth. Then forever.|He found love. The devil found Gretchen.|The one word that breaks every contract.");
ST('intolerance', "Four stories from four ages, the fall of Babylon, the Passion, the St Bartholomew's Day massacre and a modern young man facing the gallows, cut together as one flood of history.", "Love's struggle throughout the ages.", "palace/d//the walls of Babylon, elephants on the columns, a cast of thousands|village/d//a crowd gathers around a man at a wedding in Cana|city/n//Paris, 1572: the bells ring for a massacre|courtroom/d/B/a young wife hears her husband sentenced to hang|bedroom/d/A/a woman rocks a cradle, out of time", "Four ages. One cradle.|Babylon falls. Paris burns. A man waits to hang.|The race to the gallows is on.|Out of the cradle, endlessly rocking.");
ST('hospitality', "In the 1830s a young New Yorker travels south on a ramshackle early train to claim his inheritance, and walks straight into a family feud whose code says he's safe only while he's their guest.", "The feud is off. As long as he stays for dinner.", "train/d/A/a toy-like early train bumps over a wobbly track, the driver waves|mansion/d/A/a young man is invited to dinner by the family that wants to kill him|mansion/n/A/he refuses to leave the house: under its roof he cannot be shot|mountains/d/A/a chase on the cliffs, still tied to his would-be killer|river/d/A/a dive across a waterfall to catch the girl as she goes over", "He went south for a fortune.|He found a feud.|Never leave the dinner table.|One stuntman. One waterfall. No double.");
ST('bigparade', "A rich idler joins up when America enters the Great War, falls for a French farm girl in a billet village, and is marched to a front that takes everything from him.", "The war, as the men who marched saw it.", "street/d/A/a rich boy enlists in a crowd of cheering men|farm/d/A/a soldier teaches a French girl to chew gum|street/d/A/she runs alongside the trucks as the column moves out|forest/d//men walk slowly through a wood, falling one by one as the guns find them|field/d/A/a man on a crutch crosses a field toward the girl he left", "He went for the parade.|She didn't speak his language. She didn't need to.|The march into the woods.|He came back. Not all of him.");
ST('wind', "A fragile Virginia girl comes to live on the Texas prairie, where the wind never stops, a marriage she didn't want begins, and a stranger won't leave her alone.", "The wind drove her mad.", "train/d/A/a girl from Virginia rides into a sandstorm on the train west|farm/d/A/a cabin on the plains, sand pouring through every crack|farm/n/A/the wind howls; a man forces his way in|desert/n/A/she buries a body in the sand, and the wind uncovers his face|desert/n//a white horse in the clouds of a storm", "The prairie never stops blowing.|She came west for a home.|What she buried, the wind dug up.|Some storms don't pass. They move in.");
ST('chienandalou', "A man sharpens a razor on a balcony, a woman's eye is sliced, ants pour from a hand, and the logic of a dream takes over a Paris apartment for sixteen minutes.", "Once upon a time.", "apartment/n//a man sharpens a razor by moonlight|apartment/d//ants crawl from a hole in a man's palm|street/d//a woman pokes at a severed hand in the street|apartment/d//a man drags two pianos, two dead donkeys and two priests across a room|beach/d//a couple buried to their chests in sand", "Once upon a time…|Sixteen years later.|Around three in the morning.|In the spring.");
ST('earth', "In a Ukrainian village a young farmer brings the first tractor to the new collective, dances home in the dusk, and is shot by a kulak, and the village buries him with apples falling in the rain.", "The earth endures.", "farm/d//an old man dies smiling under the apple trees|field/d//a tractor rolls into the village; the farmers gather to watch|field/d//the ploughs tear up the old boundary fences|village/n//a young man dances alone down a dusty road at dusk|village/d//a funeral procession through the orchards, apples in the rain", "The old man dies under his apple tree.|The tractor is coming.|He danced home. He never got there.|The land outlasts them all.");
ST('troubleparadise', "Two elegant thieves meet in Venice, fall in love while picking each other's pockets, and then go to Paris to fleece a perfume heiress who may be harder to leave than to rob.", "The most fun you can have with a stolen wallet.", "hotel/n//a candlelit Venice dinner, two crooks swapping stolen items|ballroom/n//an opera box; a jewelled handbag goes missing|office/d//the thief hired as the heiress's secretary checks her books|mansion/n//a clock strikes the hours of a night he should have left|car/n//the thieves drive off, still stealing from each other", "He's a crook. She's a crook.|They're in love.|And the heiress is very, very rich.|Somebody's going to get robbed. Possibly of their heart.");
ST('goddess', "In 1930s Shanghai a streetwalker gives everything to keep her son in school, while a gambler who owns her takes everything she earns.", "She sold herself so he could study.", "street/n/A/a woman in a qipao waits under a streetlamp|apartment/d/A/a mother rocks her baby in a tiny rented room|school/d//other parents demand the boy be expelled|apartment/n/A/she hides her savings in a hole in the wall|prison/d/A/a woman alone in a cell, her son's picture on the wall", "A goddess of the street.|A mother in the daylight.|Everything she earns goes to his school.|And a man who takes it all.");
ST('makeway', "An elderly couple lose their house and their grown children split them up to share the burden, and they have one last afternoon together in New York before the train.", "It's not too late to tell them.", "apartment/n//five grown children argue over who has to take their parents|apartment/d//an old woman's bridge game ruins her daughter-in-law's class|hotel/n//an old couple dance in the hotel where they honeymooned|street/n//they pretend it's their wedding again|train/n//a wave from the train window, perhaps forever", "Fifty years married.|Five children. Not one room.|One last afternoon in the city.|Bring a handkerchief. Bring two.");
ST('chrysanthemums', "The adopted heir of a great kabuki family is a bad actor nobody dares tell, until a young nursemaid does, and loving her costs them both everything.", "She told him the truth. He gave his life to the stage.", "theatre/n//the audience smiles politely at a poor performance|street/n//a nursemaid walks beside him eating watermelon and tells him the truth|stage/n//years of touring with a shabby troupe in the provinces|stage/n//a triumph in Osaka; she listens from the wings|bedroom/n//she dies as the boats carry him through the city in triumph", "A famous name. A poor actor.|Only the nursemaid told him the truth.|The family threw them both out.|Years on the road for one great night.");
ST('sullivans', "A director of hit comedies wants to make a serious picture about suffering, so he goes on the road dressed as a hobo, and the road takes him further than he meant to go.", "Laughter is all some people have.", "office/d//studio bosses beg their star director to make another comedy|car/d//a hobo hitches a ride; the studio's trailer follows close behind|train/n//a director and a girl ride the rails in a boxcar|prison/d//a chain gang in a southern swamp|church/n//convicts in a country church laugh at a cartoon", "He wanted to make the real thing.|He went out to find suffering.|He found it.|There's a lot to be said for making people laugh.");
ST('shadowdoubt', "A teenage girl in a sleepy California town is thrilled when her charming uncle comes to stay, until she starts to suspect he's the man the papers call the Merry Widow Murderer.", "Her favourite uncle is coming to stay.", "train/d/A/a dark plume of smoke pulls into a small-town station|apartment/d/A/a charming uncle gives his niece a ring with someone else's initials|diner/n//a bar where a niece confronts her uncle across the booth|street/n//a library at closing time; she finds the clipping he tore out|train/d/A/a struggle in the doorway of a moving train", "Uncle Charlie's in town.|He's everyone's favourite.|Except the one who knows.|Some families have a skeleton. This one has a guest.");
ST('oddmanout', "A wounded rebel leader is hunted through one long night in a northern Irish city after a robbery goes wrong, while everyone who finds him wants something from him.", "Every hand in the city reaches for him.", "office/d//a mill robbery; a shot; a man falls from the getaway car|street/n/A/a wounded man stumbles through dark streets as rain turns to snow|bar/n//a pub full of people pretending not to see the man in the corner|apartment/n//a painter tries to capture a dying man's face|ship/n/A/the docks in the snow, his girl beside him, the police closing in", "One night. One wound.|The whole city is looking.|Some want to help. Some want the reward.|The odd man out.");
ST('heiress', "In 1840s New York a plain, shy heiress is courted by a charming young man, and her cold father is sure he's a fortune hunter; the question is whether being right is worth what it costs.", "She was taught to be cruel by masters.", "ballroom/n/A/a shy girl at a dance; a handsome young man asks her to dance|mansion/d/C/a father tells his daughter coldly what she's worth|mansion/n/A/she waits with her bags packed for a carriage that doesn't come|mansion/n/B/years later, he's back at the door|mansion/n/A/she bolts the door and takes the lamp up the stairs", "He wanted her. Or her money.|Her father knew which.|She waited by the window.|Then she learned.");
ST('aceinhole', "A cynical reporter stuck in Albuquerque finds a man trapped in a cliff dwelling and stretches out the rescue so the story keeps him on the front page, as a circus grows outside.", "The story of a man who kept his scoop alive.", "office/d//a big-city reporter talks his way into a small-town paper|desert/d//a man is trapped in a collapsed cliff dwelling|desert/d//a carnival with a Ferris wheel grows up beside the rescue|desert/n//a drill grinds slowly through the mountain for days|office/n//a dying reporter falls toward the camera in the newsroom", "A man is trapped in a cave.|A reporter is trapped in a nowhere town.|Only one of them wants out.|Step right up. The carnival's on the mountain.");
ST('countrypriest', "A sickly young priest in a poor French village keeps a diary as his parish turns against him, and finds grace in the hardest places.", "All is grace.", "church/d//a young priest arrives in a grey village|bedroom/n//he writes his diary by lamplight, eating bread soaked in wine|mansion/d//a countess and a priest argue over God and her dead son|street/d//schoolgirls snigger behind his back|street/d//a cross fills the screen at the end", "A young priest. A hostile parish.|His only companion was his diary.|His stomach is failing. His faith is not.|What does it matter? All is grace.");
ST('earlysummer', "A cheerful twenty-eight-year-old woman lives with her parents and her brother's family in postwar Kamakura, and while they plan a good marriage for her, she quietly makes her own choice.", "The family wanted to choose. She chose.", "apartment/d/A/three generations share a small house by the sea|office/d/A/a secretary jokes with her friends about marriage|apartment/n/B/a brother is shocked by his sister's choice|beach/d//two old parents sit on the dunes; the family is breaking up|field/d//a wedding procession crosses the barley fields", "The family arranged everything.|She had other plans.|One quiet decision.|And a family scatters like summer.");
ST('oharu', "An ageing woman sheltering in a temple looks at statues of Buddha and remembers a life that went from court lady to concubine to courtesan to beggar, each fall the fault of men.", "From palace to street, the life of one woman.", "church/n/A/an old woman in a temple sees a lover's face in a statue|palace/d/A/a court lady falls for a page; he is executed|palace/d/A/she bears a lord his heir and is sent away|street/n/A/she plies her trade on a dark street|village/d/A/a beggar woman walks away down the road, ringing her bell", "She was a court lady.|She was the mother of a lord's heir.|She was sold.|And still she walked on.");
ST('forbiddengames', "Her parents killed on the road in 1940, a five-year-old Paris girl is taken in by peasants and, with their young son, builds a secret cemetery for dead animals with stolen crosses.", "A child's war.", "bridge/d//refugees on a bridge; planes swoop down|farm/d//a peasant boy finds a little girl holding her dead puppy|farm/d//two children bury a mole and a chick under tiny crosses|church/n//a boy steals crosses from the church and from the hearse|village/d//a girl in a crowded station cries one name", "She lost everything in a moment.|He gave her the only thing he had.|A secret cemetery.|A child's game. A war's damage.");
ST('hulotholiday', "A gangly, polite bachelor arrives at a seaside hotel in his sputtering little car and spends one summer week accidentally ruining every guest's careful holiday.", "Nobody's on holiday with Hulot.", "car/d/A/an old car coughs its way into a seaside town|hotel/d/A/a door flaps open and every guest looks up at the wind|beach/d/A/a kayak snaps in half like a shark's jaws|hotel/n/A/a radio blares into the quiet lounge|beach/n/A/a shed full of fireworks goes off in the night", "One week by the sea.|One guest.|Everything goes wrong.|So politely.");
ST('vitelloni', "Five young men in an Italian seaside town drift through their twenties, hanging round the café, sponging off their families, dreaming of leaving, and only one does.", "Five friends who never grew up.", "beach/d//a beauty pageant in the rain; a girl faints|bar/n//five men in suits lean on the counter of a café|ballroom/n//a carnival dance; one drunk friend in a woman's mask|street/d//a man is dragged home after cheating on his young wife|train/d//the train pulls out; one of them leaves for good", "Five friends.|One summer, every summer.|They talk of leaving.|One of them did.");
ST('starborn54', "A big, drunk, fading movie star discovers a band singer and makes her a star, and as she rises, he falls.", "A woman's rise. A man's fall.", "stage/n/B/a drunk star stumbles onstage at a benefit; a singer covers for him|club/n/A/an after-hours club; a woman sings 'The Man That Got Away'|stage/n/A/a newcomer wins the top acting award; her husband arrives drunk|beach/d/B/a man walks out into the ocean and doesn't come back|stage/n/A/'This is Mrs. Norman Maine.'", "The man that got away.|A star was found.|A star was falling.|She'll always be Mrs Norman Maine.");
ST('smilessummer', "At the turn of the century, a lawyer, his young wife, his ex-mistress, her jealous count and assorted servants are invited for one country weekend that swaps them all back into the right pairs.", "One summer night has three smiles.", "theatre/n//a lawyer at the theatre watches his ex-lover on the stage|apartment/n//a count arrives at an actress's flat while the lawyer's in her nightshirt|mansion/n//a country house dinner; wine that makes lovers of strangers|mansion/n//a pistol game of Russian roulette, fired with soot|field/n//a maid and a groom tumble in the hay at dawn", "Three smiles of a summer night.|One for the young lovers.|One for the fools.|And one for the lonely.");
ST('mononcle', "Monsieur Hulot lives in a crumbling old Paris neighbourhood, and his little nephew would much rather be there with him than in his parents' absurd automatic modern house.", "A house that's all modern. An uncle who isn't.", "street/d/A/a man climbs a maze of crooked stairs to his garret|mansion/d//a fish fountain switches on only for guests|lab/d/A/a plastic hose factory spits out sausage-shaped tubes|mansion/n//two round windows in a modern house look like eyes|street/d//boys whistle at men so they walk into lampposts", "Monsieur Hulot's in the modern world.|And the modern world can't cope.|His nephew prefers him.|Who wouldn't?");
ST('hiddenfortress', "Two squabbling, greedy peasants are recruited by a mysterious general to smuggle a disguised princess and her clan's gold across enemy lines.", "Two fools, a princess, a general and a fortune.", "desert/d//two exhausted peasants squabble across a desert after a battle|mountains/d/A/a stern general shows them gold hidden in sticks of firewood|village/n//a fire festival; the princess dances with the peasants|field/d/A/a spear duel between old rival generals|palace/d//the peasants are brought before the princess in her robes", "A general. A princess. Two peasants.|And a fortune hidden in firewood.|Enemy lines in every direction.|The two greediest men alive are the only ones who can help.");
ST('kaagazphool', "A famous film director with a broken marriage finds a young woman sheltering from the rain, makes her a star, and is ruined by the gossip and his own pride.", "The paper flowers of fame.", "stage/d/A/an old man in a dark studio, remembering|street/n/B/a director gives his coat to a girl in the rain|stage/d/B/a beam of light falls across an empty studio floor|street/n/A/rumours in the press; his daughter is ashamed of him|stage/n/A/an old man dies alone in a director's chair", "He made her a star.|He couldn't keep her.|Fame is a paper flower.|And the studio lights go out one by one.");
ST('peepingtom', "A shy young focus puller in London murders women with his camera's tripod, filming their faces as they die, while the girl downstairs tries to be his friend.", "Do you know what the most frightening thing in the world is?", "street/n//a camera's viewfinder follows a woman into her room|stage/d//a body found in a trunk on a film set|apartment/n//a projection room; a young man watches his footage again and again|apartment/n//the girl downstairs watches home films of his father's experiments|apartment/n//a blind mother hears too much from the room above", "He wanted to film fear.|He had a special way of making it happen.|The film that ended a career.|Just look into the camera.");
ST('mughaleazam', "Prince Salim, heir to the Mughal throne, falls in love with the court dancer Anarkali, and the Emperor Akbar would rather go to war with his son than allow it.", "An empire against a love.", "palace/d/A/the prince returns from war in a gleaming procession|palace/n/B/a dancer twirls in the hall of mirrors|palace/d//the emperor in his robes refuses his son|battlefield/d/A/the son leads an army against his father|prison/n/B/a dancer is bricked up behind a wall", "A prince. A dancer.|An emperor's refusal.|A war between father and son.|Love sings in the hall of mirrors.");
ST('housemaid', "A piano teacher's family moves into a new two-storey house and hires a maid, who seduces the husband and then takes over the household with rat poison and a staircase.", "A maid who wanted the whole house.", "mansion/d//a family moves into a new two-storey house|apartment/n//piano lessons; a young maid watches from the stairs|apartment/n//a bottle of rat poison on the kitchen shelf|apartment/n//a child falls down the stairs|apartment/n//a husband reads his paper, then looks straight at us", "The new house is perfect.|The new maid is too perfect.|The rat poison is in the kitchen.|Don't take the stairs.");
ST('whenwomanascends', "A widowed bar hostess in Ginza is turning thirty, and every evening she climbs the stairs to work and decides whether to marry, open her own bar, or keep on.", "Every night, she climbs the stairs.", "street/n/A/a woman in a kimono looks up a narrow staircase|bar/n/A/a hostess pours drinks and listens to men|bar/n//a rival hostess has her own bar now|apartment/n/A/a proposal from a factory owner who turns out to be married|street/n/A/she climbs the stairs again and smiles at the customers", "Ginza, at dusk.|Thirty, widowed, and still working.|Every night, the same stairs.|Every night, she goes up.");
ST('vivresavie', "In twelve tableaux, a young Parisian woman who wants to be an actress drifts into prostitution, and the film watches her with a strange tenderness and then lets her go.", "My life to live.", "bar/d/A/the back of a woman's head, talking to a man at a café counter|theatre/n/A/she weeps at Falconetti's Joan of Arc|street/n/A/she walks the streets of Paris|bar/d/A/a philosopher talks to her about language and love|street/d/A/a street at the end: a car, a shot", "Twelve tableaux.|One life.|She wanted to be an actress.|Paris watched her, and looked away.");
ST('sorpasso', "A shy law student is picked up by a loud, charming braggart on a deserted Roman holiday and taken on a wild drive up the coast that changes his life in every way.", "A holiday in the fast lane.", "street/d/A/an empty Rome on the August holiday; a man in a car needs a phone|car/d/A/a convertible with a musical horn races down the Aurelia|beach/d/A/a beach club; dancing to the twist|bar/n//the shy student begins, hesitantly, to have fun|mountains/d//a car goes over a cliff by the sea", "One holiday.|One car.|One maniac at the wheel.|And one young man who learned to live.");
ST('vidassecas', "A family of drought refugees crosses the parched backlands of northeast Brazil with their dog, looking for a place to live and finding only another kind of misery.", "Barren lives.", "desert/d//a family walks under a white, burning sky|desert/d//a dog runs ahead, looking back for her family|farm/d//a cowherd works for a rancher who cheats him|prison/n//a man is beaten in jail for nothing|desert/d//the family walks on, toward somewhere", "The drought.|The road.|The dog called Baleia.|They walk on, toward the rain that never comes.");
ST('verdugo', "A Madrid undertaker marries the daughter of the state executioner, and to keep the flat that comes with the job he has to take over as executioner himself.", "A good job is hard to find.", "prison/d//an undertaker meets an executioner at a prison|apartment/d//the young couple need a flat; only the executioner gets one|street/d//a baby, a flat, and a job he never wants to do|beach/d//the call comes on a Mallorca holiday|prison/d//two guards drag a fainting executioner across a vast white courtyard", "He needed a flat.|The flat came with a job.|The job was the garrote.|Congratulations on your promotion.");
ST('iamcuba', "Four stories of Cuba before the revolution, a Havana girl, a sugarcane farmer, a student and a peasant who takes up arms, shot by a camera that seems to fly.", "I am Cuba.", "hotel/d//a camera glides off a rooftop party and dives into the pool|club/n//a bar girl in Havana and an American tourist|farm/d//a farmer sets fire to his sugarcane field|street/d//students protest; police open fire|mountains/d//peasants march to join the rebels in the mountains", "I am Cuba.|Casinos. Sugar. Revolution.|The camera floats.|You won't believe how they shot it.");
ST('pierrotfou', "A bored Parisian husband runs off with his children's babysitter, a woman with gangster friends, and their road trip to the Mediterranean turns into crime, poetry and dynamite.", "Pierrot the Madman.", "ballroom/n/A/a party lit in red, green and blue; everyone speaks in ads|car/n/A/a couple drive south through the colours of a city at night|beach/d/B/she sings on a beach; he writes in his diary|apartment/d/B/a man lies dead on her bed, scissors in his neck|beach/d/A/a man paints his face blue and wraps it in dynamite", "A man. A woman. A car.|The South of France.|Guns, books and every colour there is.|And a long blue fuse.");
ST('virginiawoolf', "A history professor and his wife invite a young couple back after a faculty party and spend the whole night tearing each other, and their guests, to shreds.", "You are cordially invited to George and Martha's for an evening of fun and games.", "apartment/n/A/a woman in a stretched cardigan mocks her husband|apartment/n/B/a man pretends to shoot his wife with a shotgun; out pops an umbrella|bar/n//a roadhouse; a dance turns into humiliation|apartment/n//the young wife is drunk on the bathroom floor|apartment/d/A/at dawn, a hushed song: who's afraid of Virginia Woolf?", "George and Martha are fighting again.|Get the guests.|Hump the hostess.|Who's afraid of Virginia Woolf?");
ST('closelywatched', "A shy young railway apprentice in the occupied Czech countryside is obsessed with losing his virginity, and almost by accident becomes part of a plot against a German ammunition train.", "Life at a very quiet station.", "train/d//a young man in a brand new uniform at a sleepy country station|train/n//a dispatcher stamps a girl's bottom with the station stamps|apartment/n//a nervous boy fails with his girl|train/d//a German train full of ammunition approaches|bridge/d//a boy on a signal post drops a bomb onto the train", "A quiet station.|A shy apprentice.|The stationmaster's rubber stamps.|And one train that won't make it through.");
ST('belledejour', "A beautiful, frigid young Parisian wife, unable to love her husband, secretly takes work in a brothel in the afternoons and lets her fantasies take her further.", "The afternoon belonged to her.", "forest/d/A/a carriage on a country road; a fantasy of being punished|apartment/d/A/a wife with a perfect home and nothing to feel|apartment/d/A/she climbs the stairs of a discreet afternoon house|street/d//a young gangster with gold teeth falls in love|apartment/n/B/a friend tells her husband everything", "A respectable wife.|Afternoons, two till five.|A gangster with gold teeth.|Her husband has no idea.");
ST('dragoninn', "In Ming China, the eunuch-run secret police try to exterminate the children of an executed general at a remote border inn, and swordsmen gather there to stop them.", "Everyone at the inn has a sword.", "desert/d//soldiers drive prisoners across a hot desert|hotel/d//a lone traveller enters an inn full of watchful killers|hotel/n//poison in the wine; a fight over a single cup|mountains/d//swordsmen leap among the rocks|desert/d//the eunuch fights his last duel among the dunes", "Everybody comes to the inn.|Nobody leaves it.|Poison in the wine. Steel under every robe.|Swords drawn.");
ST('marketa', "In medieval Bohemia, the son of a robber knight abducts a novice nun from a rival clan, and pagan and Christian, violence and love, are tangled in the snow and woods.", "Medieval cinema like no other.", "snow/d//robber knights ambush a convoy on a snowy road|forest/n//wolves in the woods, a wild boar|church/d//a novice nun meets her captor and falls into his world|village/d//a king's army surrounds the robbers' stronghold|forest/d//a woman walks away into the trees, carrying a child", "Robber knights.|A novice nun.|Wolves in the snow.|A war between a clan and a king.");
ST('nightmaud', "A Catholic engineer has decided he'll marry a blonde he saw at mass, then spends a snowy Christmas night talking Pascal, love and chance with a free-thinking divorcee.", "One night of talk. One night of temptation.", "church/d/A/an engineer at mass stares at a blonde across the aisle|bar/n/A/he runs into an old friend; they talk about Pascal's wager|apartment/n/A/snow falls; a night in a beautiful divorcee's flat|apartment/n/A/she sleeps in the bed; he sleeps on top of the covers|beach/d/A/years later, by the sea, the truth comes out", "One night, one snowfall.|Pascal's wager.|A man who knew what he wanted.|Until he didn't.");
ST('cremator', "In 1930s Prague, a soft-spoken cremator who believes his work frees souls is drawn into Nazism and decides his own half-Jewish family needs liberating too.", "Nothing to fear. Just the furnace.", "church/d/A/a gentle man in a crematorium speaks of liberating the soul|apartment/n/A/a family photograph; a husband admires his wife|bar/n//an old friend in a Nazi pin whispers about German blood|apartment/n/A/a bath; a rope; a quiet man is going to save his wife|car/d/A/a black car leaves through the fog in triumph", "Mr Kopfrkingl is very kind.|He believes in the soul.|And in the furnace.|He only wants to set his family free.");
ST('colorpomegranates', "The life of the eighteenth-century Armenian poet Sayat-Nova, told not as a story but as a book of living tableaux, from boyhood in the monastery to death.", "A life in pictures.", "church/d//pomegranates bleed red juice into a white cloth|church/d//books laid out to dry on a monastery roof|palace/d//a poet at court plays a lute|church/d//a poet becomes a monk; sheep swarm into the church|church/d//a poet lies among chickens on the floor of a church", "Pomegranates.|Lace.|A poet's soul.|A life told as a book of living pictures.");
ST('kes', "A neglected boy from a mining town in Yorkshire, bullied at school and at home, finds a kestrel and trains it, and for a while has something that's his.", "A boy and his hawk.", "field/d//a boy climbs a wall to a kestrel's nest|bedroom/n//he reads a stolen book on falconry under the covers|field/d//the kestrel swoops to the lure|school/d//a PE teacher in a football shirt cheats in the game|farm/d//a boy buries his hawk", "A boy nobody noticed.|A hawk he trained himself.|For once, something that was his.|Fly.");
ST('nightcountingyears', "In 1881 a family in Upper Egypt secretly lives off a hidden cache of royal mummies, and when the old chief dies, his son must decide what's owed to the dead and to the nation.", "Egypt's buried treasure. And its history.", "desert/d//the funeral of the head of the tribe|desert/n//the sons are shown a secret tomb of pharaohs|village/d//a merchant buys a pharaoh's jewellery|desert/n//a son goes to the authorities|river/d//mummies are loaded onto a ship, the women mourning on the bank", "A tribe with a secret.|A cave full of kings.|A son who must decide.|The night the pharaohs leave the mountain.");
ST('gimmeshelter', "The Rolling Stones' 1969 American tour ends with a free concert at Altamont speedway with Hells Angels as security, and the film watches what happened and the band watching it.", "The Stones, the Angels and the end of the sixties.", "stage/n//a band lights up Madison Square Garden|lab/d//a band watches the footage on an editing bench|field/d//a crowd camps in a dusty field for a free concert|stage/n//the Angels beat people at the edge of the stage|lab/d//a frozen frame of a man with a gun, a knife, a fall", "The biggest band in the world.|The free concert.|The Hells Angels on security.|The end of the sixties, on film.");
ST('mccabe', "A small-time gambler builds a brothel in a raw mining town in the Pacific Northwest with a hard-headed madam, and when a big company wants to buy him out, he won't sell.", "He built a town. They wanted it.", "village/d/A/a gambler in a fur coat rides into a muddy mining town|bar/n/A/a card game in a saloon full of dirty miners|apartment/n/B/a businesslike madam smokes opium and runs the accounts|church/n//the church burns while the town fights the fire|snow/d/A/a man dies alone in the falling snow", "McCabe built a town.|Mrs Miller ran it.|The company wants to buy.|He won't sell.");
ST('discreetcharm', "Six well-off friends keep trying to sit down to a nice dinner, and something always gets in the way: soldiers, ghosts, police, the curtain rising on a stage.", "They just want to have dinner.", "mansion/n//guests arrive for a dinner that's the wrong night|bar/d//a café has run out of tea, coffee and milk|mansion/n//soldiers on manoeuvres join the dinner party|stage/n//a curtain rises: the guests are on stage in a play|field/d//six friends walk down an empty country road, forever", "Dinner is served.|Not yet.|Not yet.|Six friends, one dinner, never.");
ST('dayfornight', "A film director tries to finish a melodrama at the Victorine studios in Nice while his crew and cast fall in and out of love, break down, and in one case die.", "A film about making a film.", "stage/d//a crane shot on a fake Paris street at the studio|stage/d/A/the star arrives from Hollywood|apartment/n/B/a young actor wonders whether women are magic|stage/d/C/a director with a hearing aid worries about the film|stage/d//a kitten won't drink from the saucer on cue", "A movie. A crew. A summer in Nice.|The director has a hearing aid.|The star has a broken heart.|And the cat won't drink the milk.");
ST('amarcord', "A year in the life of a 1930s Italian seaside town, its puffball seeds, its fascists, its famous beauty, its ocean liner, its snowfall, remembered by one teenage boy.", "I remember.", "village/d//puffballs drift in spring; the town burns the winter witch|school/d//teachers lecture bored teenagers|street/d//a fascist parade; a giant face of Mussolini made of flowers|ship/n//the whole town in rowboats watches a great liner pass|snow/d//a peacock opens its tail in the snow", "A seaside town, one year.|The puffballs. The liner. The snow.|The most beautiful woman in town.|I remember.");
ST('toukibouki', "In Dakar, a cowherd who rides a motorbike with horns and a university student scheme to get the money for passage to Paris, and to a life they've imagined there.", "The journey of the hyena.", "field/d//cattle are led to the slaughterhouse|street/d//a motorbike with cow horns on the handlebars|beach/d//a couple make love by the sea; a cross on the rocks|street/d//a wild scam in a rich man's house|ship/d//she boards the ship. He doesn't", "Dakar, 1973.|A motorbike with horns.|Paris, Paris, Paris.|The ship's leaving. Is he on it?");
ST('alifear', "In Munich a lonely, widowed cleaning woman in her sixties marries a much younger Moroccan guest worker, and her family, neighbours and colleagues turn on them.", "Happiness is not always fun.", "bar/n/A/an older woman sits alone in a bar full of migrant workers|bar/n/B/a young man asks her to dance|apartment/d/A/she tells her children; one of them kicks in the TV|street/d/A/two people sit alone at an outdoor café, everyone staring|hospital/d/B/an ulcer; she sits by his bed", "She's sixty. He's in his thirties.|She's German. He's Moroccan.|The neighbours have opinions.|Fear eats the soul.");
ST('manilaclaws', "A young fisherman comes to Manila to find the girlfriend who left for a job and never wrote back, and the city chews him up while he searches.", "In the claws of the city.", "city/d//a young man from the provinces arrives in the Manila streets|street/d//construction site; the foreman cheats the labourers|street/n//a skyscraper in the background; he's sleeping rough|club/n//a man works as a hustler in a gay bar|alley/n//a crowd chases a young man down an alley", "Manila.|He came looking for her.|The city found him first.|Neon, concrete and no way home.");
ST('harlancounty', "Coal miners in Kentucky go on strike against the Duke Power Company in 1973, and the film stays with them for thirteen months, through the picket line and the gunfire.", "Which side are you on?", "village/d//coal camp houses with no indoor plumbing|street/d//miners on the picket line at dawn|street/d//a truck of company gun thugs drives past the strikers|church/n//the miners' wives sing at a union meeting|church/d//a funeral for a miner shot on the picket line", "Harlan County.|Thirteen months on strike.|The women took the picket line.|Which side are you on?");
ST('threewomen', "In a California desert town, a shy girl begins working at a spa for elderly people and fixates on a chatty, self-absorbed co-worker, until their identities seem to swap.", "One woman became two. Two women became three.", "hotel/d//old people walk in the hot spring pool|hotel/d/B/a shy girl copies a co-worker's every move|apartment/n/A/a woman throws a dinner party nobody comes to|hotel/n/B/a girl falls from the balcony into the pool|desert/d//three women in a desert house", "Pinky worships Millie.|Millie never notices.|Then something changes places.|A desert dream in three parts.");
ST('manofmarble', "In the 1970s a young Polish film student makes a documentary about a 1950s bricklayer who was turned into a socialist hero, then erased, and keeps pushing when she's told to stop.", "Who was Birkut?", "office/d/A/a young director demands the archive footage|stage/d//a bricklayer sets a record for the propaganda cameras|street/d/A/a hot brick is passed to a hero, and burns his hands|apartment/d/A/she interviews a director who made his name with Birkut|street/d/A/a young woman walks fast down a long hallway", "He was a hero of labour.|Then he was erased.|A young director wants to know why.|They told her to stop. She didn't.");
ST('mariabraun', "A woman marries a soldier in a bombing raid just before he goes back to the war, and builds a fortune in the West German economic miracle while she waits for him to come home.", "She married for love. She made a fortune.", "street/d/A/a wedding in the middle of an air raid|bar/n/A/a GI bar after the war; she dances with an American|apartment/n/A/her husband returns to find her with the American; she kills him|office/d/A/she becomes indispensable to a businessman|apartment/d//a gas jet left on; an explosion", "She married him in an air raid.|She waited for him.|She got rich.|And the gas was left on.");
ST('vengeanceismine', "In 1960s Japan a con man kills two men, and for 78 days goes on the run, swindling and charming and killing his way across the country.", "Why?", "street/d//police lead a handcuffed man through a crowd|car/d//a body on a road, a truck|hotel/n//an inn run by a woman who falls for the killer|apartment/n//a father and his son's wife in a bath|mountains/d//bones thrown from a mountain freeze in the air", "Five killings.|78 days.|Charm, lies, a quiet inn.|Why?");
ST('pixote', "A ten-year-old boy in a São Paulo reformatory escapes with older boys into a life of pickpocketing, drug dealing and pimping, and becomes a killer by the time he's eleven.", "A child of the street.", "prison/d//boys in a brutal reformatory|street/d//a gang of kids snatch purses|apartment/n//a prostitute shelters the boys|apartment/n//a gun in a small boy's hand|street/d//a boy walks off along the railway line", "Pixote is ten.|He lives on the street.|He learns everything.|And nobody teaches him anything else.");
ST('rightstuff', "From the test pilots of the Mojave to the Mercury Seven astronauts, the story of how America went into space, and of the one pilot who had the right stuff but never went.", "How the future began.", "desert/d/A/a pilot breaks the sound barrier in an orange rocket plane|desert/d//seven astronauts chosen in a fanfare|lab/d/B/a man inside a tiny capsule, flames all around|desert/d//seven men walk out to a launch in their silver suits|desert/d/A/a pilot walks out of the smoke of a crashed jet, alive", "The test pilots.|The astronauts.|The one who never went up.|The right stuff.");
ST('therunner', "An orphan boy in an Iranian port city collects bottles, shines shoes and runs, and he races everything, trains, ships, other boys, toward something he can't name.", "The running boy.", "beach/d//an orphan on the shore of the Persian Gulf yells at a passing ship|street/d//he sells water and shines shoes|train/d//a boy runs alongside a train|school/d//he learns the alphabet, shouting it at the sea|field/d//boys race to a block of ice by a fire", "An orphan.|A port full of ships he'll never board.|A block of ice and a race to reach it.|He never stops running.");
ST('repentance', "The body of a Georgian town's dead mayor keeps turning up in his son's garden, and the woman who keeps digging it up tells a court why he must never be buried.", "A road that doesn't lead to a church.", "church/d//a funeral for a mayor|farm/d//the mayor's corpse is propped against a tree in the garden|courtroom/d//a woman tells why she keeps digging him up|palace/d//the mayor, a tyrant in a pince-nez, sings opera|street/d//an old woman asks the way to the church", "He was buried.|She dug him up.|And again.|What road leads to the church?");
ST('vagabond', "A young drifter is found frozen to death in a ditch in the south of France, and the people who met her on the road that winter tell what they remember.", "No roof, no law.", "field/d/A/a girl is found frozen in a ditch|street/d/A/a backpack on a winter road|farm/d//a hippie farmer gives her a place to stay|mansion/d//she camps with an old woman who laughs with her|forest/d//a festival of wine-dregs; a young woman falls", "She had no roof.|She had no law.|She died in a ditch.|Everyone she met remembers her differently.");
ST('timetolive', "A family moves from the mainland to Taiwan in 1947 meaning to go back soon, and one by one the elders die as the children grow up and realise there is no going back.", "A time to live, a time to die.", "village/d//a family in a Japanese-style wooden house in a southern town|village/d//a grandmother wants to walk back to the mainland|street/n//a teenager fights in a street gang|hospital/d//a mother dies; the boys cry|bedroom/d//a grandmother dies and the ants find her first", "A family that meant to go home.|A boy who grew up.|A grandmother who never stopped walking.|The mainland is just across the water.");
ST('sacrifice', "On his birthday, an ageing writer hears that nuclear war has broken out, and he promises God he will give up everything he has if the world can be saved.", "To save the world, a man burns his house.", "field/d/A/a man and his son plant a dead tree by the sea|mansion/n//planes roar overhead; the news of war|mansion/n/A/he kneels and prays|bedroom/n//a postman tells him to sleep with the witch|mansion/d/A/a house burns; an ambulance takes him away", "The war has come.|He prays.|He makes a promise.|And keeps it.");
ST('aurevoirenfants', "At a Catholic boarding school in occupied France, a boy discovers that the new pupil he's befriended is a Jewish boy being hidden by the priests.", "Goodbye, children.", "train/d//a boy leaves for boarding school in winter 1944|school/n//a boy notices his new friend doesn't eat pork|forest/n//two boys lost in the woods, found by German soldiers|bar/d//a restaurant; a Jewish man is thrown out|school/d//the Gestapo take the headmaster and three boys", "January, 1944.|A new boy at school.|A friend.|Au revoir, les enfants.");
ST('nayakan', "A boy who fled to Bombay after killing a policeman grows up to become the Robin Hood of the Dharavi slum and its most powerful don, until his own daughter asks what he is.", "The Godfather of Bombay.", "ship/n//a boy stows away on a boat to Bombay|street/d/A/a young man kills a cruel policeman|village/d/A/the slum gathers around its protector|apartment/d/A/a daughter asks him: are you a good man or a bad man?|street/d/A/a crowd in white, a funeral procession", "A boy from nowhere.|A slum's protector.|A daughter's question.|Are you a good man or a bad man?");
ST('wherefriendhouse', "A boy in a village in northern Iran accidentally takes his classmate's notebook home, and knowing his friend will be punished, he goes looking for the friend's house.", "A boy, a notebook, a village.", "school/d//a teacher threatens to expel a boy without his homework|village/d//a boy runs up a zigzag path between two villages|village/d//an old man won't let him finish speaking|village/n//a doorway carpenter talks about windows|school/d//a flower pressed into a notebook", "One notebook.|One friend.|One village to search.|Before the teacher finds out.");
ST('distantvoices', "A Liverpool family's memories in the 1940s and '50s, a father who beat them and the songs they sang in the pub, at the weddings and in the shelter.", "Memory is song.", "apartment/d//a family photograph: mother, father, three children|bar/n//everyone sings together in the pub|street/n//the war; an air raid; a shelter singing|apartment/d//a father beats his daughter|street/d//a wedding party in the rain", "A family.|A violent father.|The songs that got them through.|Sing, and the house stays standing.");
ST('shortfilmkilling', "A young drifter murders a Warsaw taxi driver, a rookie lawyer defends him, and the state kills him in return, both killings shown in unbearable detail.", "Thou shalt not kill.", "street/d//a drifter in a sickly green-filtered Warsaw|car/d//a taxi driver picks up a young man|field/d//a struggle at the riverbank with a rope and a stone|courtroom/d//a young lawyer loses his first case|prison/d//a young man is hanged", "A drifter kills a taxi driver.|The state kills the drifter.|A young lawyer loses his first case.|Thou shalt not kill.");
ST('thekiller', "A Hong Kong hit man who accidentally blinded a singer in a shootout takes one last job to pay for her eye operation, and ends up allied with the cop hunting him.", "One last job.", "club/n/A/a shootout in a night club; a singer is blinded by the flash|apartment/n/A/a hit man listens to her sing|bridge/d/B/a cop in a raincoat stalks his man|church/n/A/doves fly up in a church full of gunsmoke|church/n/B/two men fight back to back against an army", "One last job.|One singer he blinded.|One cop who understands him.|And a church full of doves.");
ST('millerscrossing', "In a Prohibition-era city, the right-hand man of an Irish political boss plays both sides of a gang war between his boss and an Italian rival, and the woods have a hat in them.", "Up is down. Black is white. And nobody knows who's on whose side.", "forest/d/A/a hat blows through the woods|apartment/n//a gangster in a dressing gown fends off killers with a tommy gun as his house burns|office/d//a gang leader lectures about ethics|forest/d/B/'Look into your heart!' A man begs for his life in the woods|forest/d/A/a funeral in the woods; he puts his hat back on", "Up is down.|Black is white.|Look in your heart.|And a hat blows through the woods.");
ST('daysbeingwild', "In 1960 Hong Kong, a handsome, cruel young man seduces and discards women while he searches for the birth mother who gave him away, and the clock keeps time for all of them.", "The minute you were with me.", "bar/d/A/a man asks a girl to remember a minute with him|apartment/n/B/she stands in the rain outside his flat|street/n//a policeman walks her home|train/d/A/a man's train through the Philippine jungle|apartment/n/C/a man in a low-ceilinged room combs his hair, ready to go out", "One minute.|Remember this minute.|A bird without legs.|It can only land once.");
ST('beautybeast91', "A bookish young woman in a French village takes her father's place as prisoner of a cursed Beast in his enchanted castle, and the furniture is rooting for them.", "The most beautiful love story ever told.", "village/d//a young woman sings her way through a bustling village|castle/n//a castle's candlestick and clock come to life|castle/n//an enchanted rose under a glass bell, petals falling|ballroom/n//a golden ballroom, a woman in yellow, a dance|castle/n//a mob of villagers with torches climbs to the castle", "A tale as old as time.|A beast.|A beauty.|And the candlestick has opinions.");
ST('barton', "In 1941 a New York playwright goes to Hollywood to write a wrestling picture and holes up in a peeling, sweating hotel next door to a friendly insurance salesman.", "Between Heaven and Hell, there's always Hollywood.", "hotel/d/A/a man in round glasses checks into an empty hotel|hotel/n/A/the wallpaper peels; something oozes behind it|office/d//a studio boss tells him to write a wrestling picture with that Barton Fink feeling|hotel/n/B/a fire: a big man with a shotgun shouts in the corridor|beach/d/A/a girl on the beach like the picture on the wall", "A playwright.|A hotel room.|A wrestling picture.|And a big friendly man next door.");
ST('howardsend', "In Edwardian England two idealistic sisters befriend a wealthy, practical family, and a country house becomes the centre of a long knot of love and inheritance.", "Who will inherit England?", "mansion/d//a country house with a great wych elm|apartment/d/B/a woman sits at a concert with her sister|mansion/n/A/a businessman proposes to the older sister|street/d/C/a younger sister walks off with a clerk's umbrella|mansion/d/B/she walks out in the meadow of the house she inherited", "Two sisters.|Two families.|One house.|Only connect.");
ST('shortcuts', "Over a few days in Los Angeles, two dozen people collide in stories of adultery, death, a cake, a dead body in a river and an earthquake.", "Twenty-two characters. One city.", "city/n//helicopters spray the city against the medfly|river/d//fishermen find a dead woman in the river and go on fishing|street/d//a boy is hit by a car on his birthday|kitchen/d//a baker keeps calling about a cake nobody picks up|city/d//an earthquake shakes everyone", "Los Angeles.|Twenty-two people.|A cake nobody collects.|And one earthquake.");
ST('remainsday', "A devoted English butler in the 1930s serves his lordship as he flirts with the Nazis, and in his perfect service never admits his love for the housekeeper.", "A great house. A great butler. A great love unspoken.", "mansion/d/A/a butler polishes the silver while the master meets the Germans|kitchen/d/B/a housekeeper puts flowers in his pantry|mansion/n/A/his father dies upstairs; he keeps serving the guests|bedroom/n/B/she asks what book he's reading|beach/n/A/a pier, a bus, and the lights come on for them", "A great house.|A great butler.|A great love, never spoken.|The remains of the day.");
ST('naked93', "An unemployed, brilliant, foul-mouthed man escapes Manchester for London, and over a few nights wanders the city talking at everyone he meets.", "Johnny's on the loose.", "alley/n/A/a man runs out of an alley after an assault in Manchester|car/n/A/he steals a car and drives to London|street/n/A/a nighttime walk through the empty streets|apartment/n/A/he talks the apocalypse with a security guard in an empty office|street/d/A/he limps off down the road alone", "Johnny's in London.|He's brilliant.|He's terrifying.|And he's not going to stop talking.");
ST('puppetmaster', "The life of Taiwan's great puppeteer Li Tian-lu from his birth to the end of the Japanese occupation, told partly by the old man himself.", "A life in puppet theatre.", "theatre/d//a puppet show in a village square|village/d//a young man joins a travelling troupe|theatre/d//puppet propaganda for the Japanese army|village/d//a family dies of malaria|theatre/d//an old man tells his story to the camera", "A puppeteer.|An occupation.|A life.|The puppets outlived the empire.");
ST('burntsun', "On a lazy summer day in 1936, a revolutionary hero's family welcomes a charming guest at their dacha, who has come on behalf of Stalin.", "A summer day in 1936.", "farm/d/A/a famous colonel lies in a steam bath at his dacha|farm/d//an old lover arrives in disguise|field/d/A/a colonel rides out to stop tanks trampling the wheat|car/d/A/a black car drives off with the hero in the back|field/d//a ball of fire rolls over the fields", "A hero.|A dacha.|A summer.|And Stalin's sun burning down.");
ST('sensesensibility', "When their father dies, the Dashwood sisters are left with almost nothing, and the sensible elder and the passionate younger find love the hard way.", "Lose your heart and come to your senses.", "mansion/d/A/a mother and daughters move to a small cottage|field/d/B/a girl twists her ankle in the rain; a dashing man carries her home|mansion/d/C/a shy man stutters a confession|ballroom/n/B/a ball where her love cuts her dead|church/d/B/a wedding in a village church", "Two sisters.|One sense.|One sensibility.|Love, the hard way.");
ST('underground95', "In Belgrade during WWII, a black marketeer hides his friend and others in a cellar making weapons and keeps them there for decades, convincing them the war never ended.", "Once upon a time there was a country.", "city/n/A/a brass band plays as bombs fall on Belgrade|apartment/n/B/a man in a cellar building weapons for decades|stage/d/A/a war film made about their legend|ballroom/n/B/an underground wedding; a monkey in a tank|river/d//an island floats away on the Danube", "Once upon a time there was a country.|A cellar.|A war that never ended.|Because nobody told them.");
ST('breakingwaves', "In a strict Presbyterian village on the Scottish coast, a simple, devout young woman marries an oil rig worker, and when he's paralysed she makes a terrible sacrifice for him.", "Love is a mighty power.", "church/d/A/a young woman stands before the church elders|church/d/A/she talks to God and answers in his voice|hospital/d/B/a paralysed man asks his wife to sleep with other men|ship/d/A/she goes to a ship; the sailors are waiting|ship/d//bells ring out from the sky above the rig", "Bess loved Jan.|Jan was hurt.|She would do anything.|And the bells rang in the sky.");
ST('happytogether', "Two men from Hong Kong break up and make up in Buenos Aires, on a trip that was meant to take them to the waterfalls at Iguazu.", "Let's start over.", "apartment/d/A/a lamp with a picture of the waterfalls on it|club/n/B/a tango bar where one of them dances with strangers|apartment/n/A/a cramped room, one bed, one smashed hand|kitchen/n//a man works in a kitchen, saving for the ticket home|river/d/A/the falls at Iguazu, alone", "Buenos Aires.|Two men.|Let's start over.|The waterfall is still waiting.");
ST('tastecherry', "A middle-aged man drives around the dusty hills outside Tehran looking for someone who'll bury him under a cherry tree if he succeeds in taking his own life.", "The taste of cherry.", "car/d//a man in a Range Rover picks up a young soldier|mountains/d//winding dirt roads around the hills of Tehran|car/d//a seminarian tells him suicide is a sin|lab/d//a taxidermist tells him about tasting a mulberry|field/d//the film crew in the hills; spring, soldiers marching", "One man.|One question.|One cherry tree.|Will you bury me?");
ST('thinredline', "On Guadalcanal in 1942, an American rifle company is sent up a hill against a hidden Japanese position, and the men's inner voices ask why nature is at war with itself.", "Every man fights his own war.", "beach/d/A/a soldier lives with islanders on a Pacific beach|ship/d//landing craft carry the company to Guadalcanal|field/d//men crawl uphill through tall grass toward a bunker|field/d/C/a colonel orders a frontal assault|forest/d/A/a man faces the enemy alone in a clearing", "Every man fights his own war.|What is this war in the heart of nature?|A hill. A company. A clearing.|The Thin Red Line.");
ST('festen', "At a wealthy family's sixtieth birthday celebration at their country hotel, the eldest son stands up to give a toast and accuses his father of abuse.", "Let's all raise a toast.", "hotel/d//a family arrives at the father's country hotel|hotel/n//the eldest son taps his glass for a speech|hotel/n//the guests go on eating as if nothing happened|hotel/n//the cooks hide the guests' car keys|hotel/d//breakfast: the father is asked to leave", "The father's birthday.|The son's speech.|The guests keep eating.|Somebody hid the car keys.");
ST('ratcatcher', "During the 1973 bin strike in Glasgow, a twelve-year-old boy who accidentally drowned his friend in the canal dreams of escape to a new housing estate at the edge of a wheatfield.", "Childhood in a dustbin summer.", "river/d//two boys fight by the canal|street/d//piles of rubbish bags in the streets of the estate|bedroom/n//a boy listens to his parents' fights|field/d//a boy climbs through the window of an unfinished house into a wheatfield|river/d//a boy steps into the canal", "Glasgow, 1973.|The bin strike.|A canal.|And a window that opens onto a field of wheat.");
ST('topsyturvy', "In 1884 Gilbert and Sullivan's partnership is falling apart, until a Japanese exhibition in London inspires a new comic opera called The Mikado.", "The story of a masterpiece.", "theatre/n/B/a composer ill backstage as the audience cheer|office/d/A/a librettist and a composer argue|street/d/A/a Japanese exhibition in Knightsbridge; a sword on the wall|stage/d/C/an actor fears his song will be cut|stage/n//The Mikado's opening night", "Gilbert.|Sullivan.|The Mikado.|The show must go on. Somehow.");
ST('mission99', "Five hired bodyguards with nothing in common are assigned to protect a triad boss from an assassin, and slowly become a team.", "Five men. One mission.", "street/d//a triad boss is shot at|club/n/A/five bodyguards meet at a bar|street/d//a shootout in a shopping centre; every man stands still and fires|office/d//the men play football with a ball of paper|street/n//a final job: one of them must die", "Five bodyguards.|One boss.|Stand still and fire.|And a paper football between shifts.");
ST('insider', "A tobacco company executive blows the whistle on his industry's lies to a 60 Minutes producer, and both men lose almost everything when the network gets cold feet.", "Two men driven to tell the truth.", "office/d/A/a scientist is fired from a tobacco company|hotel/n/B/a TV producer meets a frightened man in a hotel room|interview/d/A/a man answers questions in front of the cameras|car/n/A/a car follows him home|newsroom/d/B/a producer fights his network to air the story", "One man knew the truth.|One man wanted to tell it.|The network got scared.|They both paid.");
ST('amoresperros', "A car crash in Mexico City links three stories: a young man who fights his brother's dog for money, a supermodel and her dog, and a homeless hit man and his dogs.", "Love is a bitch.", "car/d/A/a wild car chase with a bleeding dog in the back seat|alley/n//a dogfight in a ring of shouting men|apartment/d//a model's dog vanishes under the floorboards|street/d//a homeless man with a cart and a pack of dogs|street/d//the crash at the intersection", "Love.|Dogs.|A crash at an intersection.|Three lives that never meet, until they do.");
